    "body": "My two cents: I second @sideshowbarker here. This make me think of DITA way of writing documentation: parts of a document are sufficient on their own and target audiences (there typically are multiple) are in mind. Also, imagine a documentation tool extracting parts for summaries (what I’m planing to do for some other standards). Without Sideshowbarker proposal, extracting this reference box, makes it incorrect. Or if really one want to keep the implementers point of view, then may it could say “for implementers: nothing ; for others: see prose.”",
