    "body": "> The extracted excerpt is totally correct; you're just not understanding what a content model is.\r\n\r\nI understand it’s written “content model”, the issue is not there, it’s in the adequacy with how this kind of reference is read. As I tried to explain in the issue’s thread, the issue is that without wording on the syntax, the wording on the content model will very likely be read like applying to both, because we are used to start with syntax first, then meaning after or else with both wording coming together.\r\n\r\nIf there was an explicit forward reference to something else, this would be fine. Just that the people involved here seems to not agree on the wording to use for this forward reference.",
